{#
  What We Do. Composes the frame and locked components; copy in front matter.

  OPENING: the figure breaks the container and runs to the right edge of the
  viewport, starts a step below the text, and a dashed survey rule crosses out
  of the text column and 160px into it. The image attributes are the file's TRUE intrinsic
  size, 1280x853, not the 440x320 box it used to be drawn in: the frame no
  longer fixes a height, so the attribute ratio is what reserves the space, and
  the old pair reserved a 1.375 box for a 1.5 image. See the page CSS.

  ALT-GLYPH: exactly one on this page, the O in the "Get Found" group header.
  It is the earned swap: found means located, and the target device is the mark
  for a located thing. Per character on that O only, never word-level, since
  ss10 would bleed the dot onto other letters. "Get Built" and "Stay Ahead"
  stay plain, and the `glyph` flag in front matter is what gates it, so a new
  group cannot pick one up by accident.

  HIERARCHY: service names run a step above their descriptions rather than
  level with them. See the note in the page CSS for what the handoff had.

  No pricing anywhere on this page, by instruction and by CLAUDE.md, which
  keeps pricing out of generated copy entirely.
#}
{% from "components/container.njk" import container %}
{% from "components/section.njk" import section %}
{% from "components/button.njk" import button %}
{% from "components/icon.njk" import icon %}

{% call section(class="cs-intro-band", containerClass="cs-intro", orient="Search everywhere") %}
  <div>
    <h1 class="cs-intro__headline">{{ intro.headline }}</h1>
    <p class="cs-intro__lede">{{ intro.lede }}</p>
    <div class="cs-intro__rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  </div>
  <div class="cs-intro__figure">
    <img src="{{ site.cdn }}cs-img-bee-1-landscape.webp"
         alt="Bee finding the bloom, reach and being found"
         width="1280" height="853" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async">
    <div class="cs-rule cs-rule--intro-v" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  </div>
{% endcall %}

{% call container(class="pb-22", orient="What you get") %}
  <ul class="cs-outcomes">
    {% for outcome in outcomes %}
      <li class="cs-outcome">
        <div class="cs-outcome__head">
          {{ icon(outcome.icon, size=22) }}
          <h2 class="cs-outcome__title">
            {%- if outcome.glyph -%}
              Get F<span class="alt-dot">o</span>und
            {%- else -%}
              {{ outcome.title }}
            {%- endif -%}
          </h2>
        </div>
        <ul class="cs-services">
          {% for service in outcome.services %}
            <li class="cs-service">
              <p class="cs-service__name">{{ service.name }}</p>
              <p class="cs-service__desc">
                {{ service.desc }}
                {%- if service.linkUrl %} <a href="{{ service.linkUrl }}">{{ service.linkText }}</a>.{% endif %}
              </p>
            </li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
{% endcall %}

<div class="cs-trellis">
  <div class="cs-rule cs-rule--trellis cs-rule--trellis-l" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="cs-rule cs-rule--trellis cs-rule--trellis-r" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  {% call container() %}
    <img class="cs-trellis__figure"
         src="{{ site.cdn }}cs-img-trellis-1-portrait.webp"
         alt="Trellis, the built framework growth climbs"
         width="1120" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
  {% endcall %}
</div>

{% call container(narrow=true, class="cs-statement py-22", orient="The approach") %}
  <p>{{ statement }}</p>
{% endcall %}

{% call container(class="cs-close") %}
  <p class="cs-close__note">{{ close }}</p>
  {{ button("Start a conversation", href="/contact/") }}
{% endcall %}
